  "about": "quantum_from_deltas(deltas_ns) ignores zero deltas and returns None below QUANTUM_MIN_DELTAS (16) non-zero deltas. Otherwise, for k = 1..=QUANTUM_MAX_DIVISOR (64) while d_min / k is at least QUANTUM_FLOOR_NS (1000), it walks the sorted non-zero deltas keeping a running span S and step count N, assigns each delta n = round-half-up(d * N / S) steps, and accepts the first k under which every delta lies within q/QUANTUM_TOL_DEN (16) + min(QUANTUM_SLACK_NS (512), q/64) of n * q, q being S/N held as a rational. It returns the whole-us value nearest S/N when that explains the span within 512 ns, else S/N rounded half-up to the ns, and None when no k fits. All arithmetic is on integers. A face that takes the GCD of whole-us deltas (G-17 as first drafted) fails p1 (16667000), p2 and p6 (1000). A face that drops the us snap fails p4 (1000016) and p5 (99988). The rfp_source_grid row models the 16 667 us grid read from Firefox source (likely; the call site was not read); p1 and p2 model a 1000/60 ms grid. No wall value, domain or bound enters this function.",
